## Statement

How many four-digit numbers (from $1000$ to $9999$) have four different digits?

## Hint

Choose the digits one at a time, starting with the first.

## Solution

- The first digit can be any of $1,\dots,9$: $9$ choices (it cannot be $0$).
- The second digit can be any digit except the first, including $0$: $9$ choices.
- The third digit: $8$ choices.
- The fourth digit: $7$ choices.

By the multiplication principle, there are $9\cdot9\cdot8\cdot7=4536$ such numbers.
